  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 210 AM CDT Sat Jul 4 2026\n\nThere will be a low chance for showers and thunderstorms across the \nCoastal Plains Saturday along the sea breeze. Anything that develops \nis expected to be short lived with low accumulations. As we head \ninto next week, a mid-level ridge is expected to move in which will \nkeep us warm and maintain our rain chances on the lower end. \n\nAbove normal temperature combining with ample low-level moisture \nwill promote heat index values between 100-110 degrees through the \nweekend and into early next week. Please use caution if you're \nworking or playing outside or spending time outdoors for \nIndependence Day. Take plenty of breaks, drink water, and don't \nforget sunscreen (and mosquito repellent).\n\nMore heat safety information can be found at weather.gov/heat",
